      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T12:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Device_schema_directory yields the path it prepared, but this reads self.SCHEMA_DIRECTORY instead, so the directory that gets seeded and the directory the connector is configured with are two independent values. A subclass that overrides only the fixture gets an unseeded cache and still passes, since configure_device_in_netconf defaults schema_directory to /tmp/schema. Could this build the kwargs from the device_schema_directory value and drop the class attribute?",
      "revId": "69e49b04b0b54243937ff8d5cba876c2e025fa57",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cbb0245_438e4f25",
        "filename": "tests/suites/clustering/clustering_crud_suite.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 9422
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T07:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the kwargs are built from the value device_schema_directory yields, and the SCHEMA_DIRECTORY class attribute is gone, so there is only one value and seeding can no longer diverge from configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "39a828ba_ee482344",
      "revId": "69e49b04b0b54243937ff8d5cba876c2e025fa57",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
