        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T12:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This step and the delete at line 410 are the two attributed to bug 4968, and the helper retries the write up to 120 times at 1s intervals. An intermittent 4968 regression now passes green with no tracker link, where before a single failed PUT failed the test. Could we keep the retry on the create only, or pass a small retry_count to both, so a known-bug step still fails fast?",
      "revId": "69e49b04b0b54243937ff8d5cba876c2e025fa57",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96193ccf_3493a9a2",
        "filename": "tests/suites/clustering/clustering_crud_suite.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 361,
      "author": {
        "id": 9422
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T07:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added DATA_OP_RETRY_COUNT \u003d 10 in the shared module and passed it to create/modify/delete. The transient cleared in two or three attempts when measured, so ten is enough for it while a genuine 4968 regression now fails in about ten seconds instead of two minutes.\n(The library default of 120 stays for the outage suites, where a write after a member kill genuinely needed minutes.)",
      "parentUuid": "6b120a49_1083732d",
      "revId": "69e49b04b0b54243937ff8d5cba876c2e025fa57",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
